-- The converse and the H1 form of the Serre criterion (2026-10-30).
-- Seven modules: clearing/killing along a square of equivalences and back
-- along a ring map (SerreLambdaElementarySquare); the lambda-criterion,
-- model => lambda, on every chart open pi(D h) (SerreLambdaModel); lambda
-- at the top of X read on X|1 (SerreLambdaTop); lambda_(1,g) on an affine
-- X for a quasi-coherent module, by refinement and pure descent
-- (SerreAffineLocalisation); a torsor moved along an affine chart with a
-- model (SerreTorsorChart); the converse and the criterion as an
-- equivalence (SerreAffineConverse); H1 vanishing on one or every affine
-- cover (SerreCechVanishing). Openings are structural carriers, the slice,
-- chart and scalar-restriction maps used by definition, and Trunc.carrier;
-- no localisation quotient, gluing or extensionality construction is
-- reopened.
